    {
      "id": "s0002",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "label-parameter-version¶",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0003",
      "kind": "heading",
      "text": "Description¶",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "A parameter label is a user-defined alias to help you manage different versions of a parameter. When you modify a parameter, Amazon Web Services Systems Manager automatically saves a new version and increments the version number by one. A label can help you remember the purpose of a parameter when there are multiple versions.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Parameter labels have the following requirements and restrictions.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "A version of a parameter can have a maximum of 10 labels.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "You can’t attach the same label to different versions of the same parameter. For example, if version 1 has the label Production, then you can’t attach Production to version 2.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "You can move a label from one version of a parameter to another.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "You can’t create a label when you create a new parameter. You must attach a label to a specific version of a parameter.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0010",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "If you no longer want to use a parameter label, then you can either delete it or move it to a different version of a parameter.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "A label can have a maximum of 100 characters.",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Labels can contain letters (case sensitive), numbers, periods (.), hyphens (-), or underscores (_).",
      "protected": []
    },
    {
      "id": "s0013",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Labels can’t begin with a number, “[[p0]] “ or “[[p1]] “ (not case sensitive). If a label fails to meet these requirements, then the label isn’t associated with a parameter and the system displays it in the list of InvalidLabels.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "aws"
          }
        },
        {
          "token": "[[p1]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "ssm"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0014",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "Parameter names can’t contain spaces. The service removes any spaces specified for the beginning or end of a parameter name. If the specified name for a parameter contains spaces between characters, the request fails with a [[p0]] error.",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "code",
            "text": "ValidationException"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s0015",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "text": "See also: [[p0]]",
      "protected": [
        {
          "token": "[[p0]]",
          "inline": {
            "tag": "link",
            "text": "AWS API Documentation",
            "href": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/goto/WebAPI/ssm-2014-11-06/LabelParameterVersion"
          }
        }
      ]
